WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.837
-Not a single Republican voted
for the historic

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:07.773
$1.9 trillion COVID relief bill
passed by the Senate this week.

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:09.808
And in fact, Republicans spent
most of the weekend

00:00:09.808 --> 00:00:12.946
trying to derail it while
still whining about Dr. Seuss.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:15.681
For more on this,
it's time for a closer look.

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:19.418 align:start size:34% position:66% line:0%
♪♪

00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:21.787
The past few months have offered
a deeply-revealing look

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:23.389
at the state of
American democracy

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:25.724
and the course it could take
over the next few years

00:00:25.724 --> 00:00:26.859
without major reforms.

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:29.094
On the one hand,
we saw a political faction

00:00:29.094 --> 00:00:31.197
which represents a minority
of American voters

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.366
try to overturn
an election they lost

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.634
and then sow a violent
insurrection to interfere

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.937
with the lawful counting
of electoral votes.

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:41.274
And then about two months later,
we saw 50 Senate Democrats,

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:44.276
who represent about
41 million more Americans

00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:46.212
than the 50 Senate Republicans,

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.848
vote to deliver one of the
largest rescue bills in history,

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.750
which has been massively
popular in poll after poll.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.086
And not a single Republican
joined them

00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:55.588
in the Senate or in the House.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:58.191
They were too busy
doing dumb [bleep] like this.

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:01.828
-"Green Eggs and Ham"
by Dr. Seuss.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:07.733
"I am Sam.
I am Sam. Sam, I am."

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:11.871
"Do you like green eggs
and ham?"

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.106
"I do not like them, Sam, I am."

00:01:14.106 --> 00:01:17.743
"You do not like them.
Say -- so you say.

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:20.246
Try them, try them,
and you may."

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:26.752
"Say! I like green eggs and ham.
I do. I like them Sam, I am."

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:29.455
"I do so like green eggs
and ham.

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:33.726
Thank you. Thank you Sam, I am."

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.361
Enjoy your day.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.664
-Well I can't now.

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:39.031
Not after that performance.

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:40.466
There's nothing cringier
than watching

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:43.603
a grown adult
in a suit read Dr. Seuss

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.205
to an empty room
with no children around.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.374
Is that the Fox News version
of "Reading Rainbow?"

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.142
"Reading Rainblows?"

00:01:50.142 --> 00:01:51.845
This is what a hostage video
would look like

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.879
if Barney was the kidnapper.

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:56.182
Serious Stockholm Syndrome when
you get kidnapped by Barney --

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.850
you're so mad
when you get rescued.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:02.021
You don't understand.
I love him. He loves me.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:05.925
Most importantly, green eggs and
ham isn't canceled, ya goober!

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.560
It's on Amazon's
best seller list,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.661
thanks to all your whining.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.929
I wouldn't be surprised if
we find out

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.632
the Seuss people did this
just to move more product.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:13.900
"No one's buying our books."

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.169
[ Dramatically ] "Say we're
pulling them for racism.

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:19.839
They will fly off the shelves!"

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.541
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.442
[ Normally ] No one
canceled anything.

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:25.778
The copyright holder
voluntarily withdrew

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.147
six books from publication

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.215
because of racist imagery
and language.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.784
The books include titles
like "The Cat's Quizzer"

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.186
and "McElligot's Pool,"

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:35.855
which I'm guessing
is where Steve Bannon drowned.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:38.224
When it comes to Fox News
and the Republican Party,

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.326
their brand is overreaction.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.695
Take their feigned outrage
over "The Muppet Show."

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.530
Disney decided to add
a disclaimer

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.666
in front of an episode
with a Confederate flag,

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:47.700
among others.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.270
But it's Fox News,
not Fox Nuance.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:53.573
So they act like Kermit the Frog
was thrown in an unmarked van,

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:54.974
never to be seen
or heard from again.

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:56.709
You can still see the episode.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.911
And just to show
you cancel culture isn't real,

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:00.546
it stars Johnny Cash,

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:06.986
who shot a man in Reno
just to watch him die.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.988
No second reason.

00:03:09.988 --> 00:03:11.323
Anyway, the point is this

00:03:11.323 --> 00:03:13.125
is what our
two major political factions

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.627
have decided to spend
their time on --

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.663
one's trying to deliver
a massively popular relief bill

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:18.964
that includes direct payments,

00:03:18.964 --> 00:03:20.933
expanded child
and unemployment benefits,

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:22.634
and funding for vaccinations.

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:25.271
And another is holding
story time for ghost children

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:28.173
in a library of the damned,
trying to overturn the election,

00:03:28.173 --> 00:03:31.643
and trying to prevent people
from voting in the next one.

00:03:31.643 --> 00:03:34.112
The tidal wave of anti-voting
legislation unleashed

00:03:34.112 --> 00:03:36.749
by Republican state legislatures
over the past few weeks

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.684
has gotten so insane
that Georgia Republicans

00:03:38.684 --> 00:03:41.053
have proposed a series of bills
that would,

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:43.388
among other things,
target Black voters,

00:03:43.388 --> 00:03:46.825
ban no-excuse absentee ballots,
roll back Sunday voting,

00:03:46.825 --> 00:03:49.095
and ban what is known
as "line warming,"

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:51.163
the practice of having
volunteers provide water,

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:53.766
snacks, chairs and other
assistance to voters in line.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:57.036
Holy [bleep]. They're trying to
ban voters from having water,

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.537
snacks, and chairs?

00:03:58.537 --> 00:03:59.739
Republicans want to turn voting

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.774
into one of those
extreme radio station contests

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.476
where whoever goes the longest
without peeing

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:06.178
gets two backstage passes
to an Aerosmith concert.

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:08.848
If the GOP had their way,
there would be one polling place

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:11.383
in every state open
for like three hours a week,

00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:13.018
and instead of a school,
it would be at

00:04:13.018 --> 00:04:16.589
the end of an "American Ninja
Warrior"-style obstacle course.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.557
If you don't bring
three forms of ID,

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:21.327
you get knocked off the platform
by a giant foam hand.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:22.561
Also, I love
how the party of freedom

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:24.429
wants to make it illegal
to give someone a snack.

00:04:24.429 --> 00:04:26.098
They're canceling snacks.

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:28.234
Quick get Kevin McCarthy
on YouTube

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:31.003
so he can read the ingredients
on a pack of Oreos.

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:32.738
[ Imitating Kevin McCarthy]
Unbleached enriched flour,

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:36.976
canola oil or palm oil.
Enjoy your day,

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.377
[ Normally ] I guess in
the GOP's America,

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:39.846
voters aren't allowed to
drink water

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.681
unless it's from
McElligot's pool.

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:43.349
So that's the central story

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:44.784
of our political culture
at the moment.

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:47.019
One coalition is becoming
increasingly deranged

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:48.454
and extreme
and anti-democracy,

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:51.089
and the other is still committed
to competent governance.

00:04:51.089 --> 00:04:53.192
And look, that doesn't mean
this bill is perfect --

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.895
far from it. For one thing,
the bill keeps the expanded

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:59.565
unemployment benefits at $300
rather than the original $400

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:00.899
Democrats had aimed for,

00:05:00.899 --> 00:05:02.768
and it sets them
to expire by Labor Day --

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:05.538
a deal forced by moderate
Democrat Joe Manchin,

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:08.007
for reasons no one
seems to understand

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.775
on either side of the aisle.

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:11.410
When asked
what Manchin's issue was,

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.712
his fellow moderate Democrat,
Jon Tester, said,

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:16.515
"I don't know. I really don't."

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:18.684
Republican Shelley Moore Capito
said,

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:20.787
"I have no idea
what he's doing."

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:23.188
Cool, because that's what
you want in a Senate

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:25.024
that's split 50/50 --
a wild card.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:26.592
So, I know that photo
right there was taken

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:28.861
just as Manchin found out
he was a Democrat.

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:31.064
[ Bewildered ] "I am?
Oh, man, in West Virginia?

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:33.332
Hoohoohoo, good luck to me."

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:34.933
[ Normally ] It's weird to hear
senators talking about

00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:37.069
one of their colleagues
the way baseball announcers

00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:38.971
talk about a streaker.
"And now he's wrestling

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:41.107
the T-shirt gun away
from the Philly fanatic.

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:42.775
Do you know what he is doing
out there, Buck?"

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:45.011
"I really don't. Either we're
all getting T-shirts

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:47.947
or we're going to see a man get
his nuts tasered off."

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:49.048
A 50/50 split means

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:50.449
all the Democrats have to
stick together.

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:52.518
You can't have one guy
splintering off the last minute.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:55.521
It's like an escape room where
everyone's focused on the clue

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:57.357
hidden under the genie's lamp,
and one guy's like,

00:05:57.357 --> 00:05:59.826
"I bet I can just
kick this door down."

00:05:59.826 --> 00:06:01.560
"Devin, can you just
use your brain for once?"

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.496
"Uh, and waste these quads?
No, thank you."

00:06:04.496 --> 00:06:06.766
Then there's the fact that a
group of Democratic senators

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:09.635
and Independent Angus King
split off and joined Republicans

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:12.171
in voting down a proposal
to raise the minimum wage

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:15.674
to $15 an hour, which is wildly
popular in polls and something

00:06:15.674 --> 00:06:17.376
President Biden campaigned on.

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:20.980
One member of that group,
Arizona senator Kyrsten Sinema,

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:24.150
has gotten a lot of criticism
for the enthusiastic thumbs down

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.484
she gave the bill on the Senate
floor,

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.687
like a judge on
"America's Got Talent"

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:30.156
after an 8-year-old
bombs doing stand up.

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:32.124
"Sorry, Tyler,
but the 90s called --

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:35.395
they want
their joke format back."

00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:37.263
But let's not lose sight
of the senators

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:39.365
from safe Democratic seats
like Chris Coons

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:42.301
and Tom Carper in Delaware,
who voted it down for no reason

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.303
other than they don't like it
on policy grounds.

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:45.238
I mean, what's wrong
with you guys?

00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:46.405
You're not going to face any

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:47.840
serious Republican opposition,

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.075
and yet you're still siding
with them?

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:50.209
Watching these guys is like

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:53.112
watching LeBron play defense
against himself.

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:54.647
By the way, playing defense
against himself

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:56.949
is the only way he'll ever
get called for a foul.

00:06:56.949 --> 00:07:00.486
I'm just kidding. I love him
and I want him to be my friend.

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:02.655
With all that said,
it's important not to understate

00:07:02.655 --> 00:07:04.757
the truly seismic nature
of this bill

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:07.760
and all the incredible good
it will do for millions of poor

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.495
and working-class Americans.
For one thing,

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:11.763
it's way bigger than
the 2009 stimulus,

00:07:11.763 --> 00:07:14.166
and that's a good thing
because the 2009 stimulus

00:07:14.166 --> 00:07:15.501
wasn't nearly enough.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:18.036
This bill sends about
$350 billion

00:07:18.036 --> 00:07:20.806
in state and local governments
to keep services running,

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:23.609
save pensions and schools
and public transit,

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:26.345
and keep people employed.
It sends out direct payments

00:07:26.345 --> 00:07:28.080
to about 85% of Americans,

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.417
and it expands unemployment
benefits and child benefits.

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:34.120
One study suggested that
the bill will reduce poverty

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.190
by a third, lifting nearly
13 million Americans out of it,

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:40.259
and that child poverty would
be reduced by more than half.

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:43.128
Meanwhile, for a family of four
with one working parent

00:07:43.128 --> 00:07:44.463
and one who remains unemployed

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:46.198
because
of childcare constraints,

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:48.734
the benefits could total more
than $12,000.

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:51.170
But what about the tax credit
for high earners

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.773
who use S-corporations to buy
fine art for their catamarans?

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:55.674
Who will think of
the catamarans?!

00:07:55.674 --> 00:07:59.378
Anyway, the point is, this is
a flawed but really good bill

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:00.880
that delivers
desperately-needed help

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:03.549
to the people who need it most,
on a scale that's necessary

00:08:03.549 --> 00:08:05.318
to make an actual difference
in the economy

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:06.752
and in people's lives.
And that, of course,

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:08.621
means Republicans did everything
they could to derail it

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:10.990
with [bleep] like
Texas Senator Ted Cruz,

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.825
who offered an amendment
to stop the checks

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:14.793
from going to
undocumented immigrants,

00:08:14.793 --> 00:08:16.795
even though the bill
doesn't do that anyway,

00:08:16.795 --> 00:08:19.899
and he was immediately rebuffed
by Illinois Senator Dick Durbin.

00:08:19.899 --> 00:08:23.201
-Mr. President, moments ago,
the Democrats in this chamber

00:08:23.201 --> 00:08:28.874
just voted to send $1,400
stimulus checks to murderers,

00:08:28.874 --> 00:08:33.879
to rapists, and child molesters
incarcerated in prison.

00:08:33.879 --> 00:08:36.949
This amendment before us today

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:38.984
provides that
the stimulus checks

00:08:38.984 --> 00:08:42.187
should not go to illegal aliens
in this country.

00:08:42.187 --> 00:08:45.491
Should your money --
should taxpayer money be sent?

00:08:45.491 --> 00:08:49.327
$1,400 to every illegal alien in
America.

00:08:49.327 --> 00:08:52.564
-Mr. President, the statement
of the senator from Texas

00:08:52.564 --> 00:08:58.337
is just plain false.
False! Let me be clear.

00:08:58.337 --> 00:09:02.574
Undocumented immigrants do not
have Social Security numbers

00:09:02.574 --> 00:09:06.879
and they do not qualify for
stimulus relief checks, period.

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:08.981
And for you to stand up there
and say the opposite

00:09:08.981 --> 00:09:11.883
is just to rile people up
over something that's not true.

00:09:11.883 --> 00:09:13.352
-Will the senator yield
for a question?

00:09:13.352 --> 00:09:14.953
-No, I won't.

00:09:14.953 --> 00:09:18.691
It is not true. And we know
what's going on here.

00:09:18.691 --> 00:09:20.125
They want to be able
to give speeches

00:09:20.125 --> 00:09:23.629
and say the checks go
to undocumented people.

00:09:23.629 --> 00:09:25.730
-Cruz is so bad at this,
he can't even be subtle

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:27.299
about his [bleep]
fear-mongering.

00:09:27.299 --> 00:09:30.302
"Democrats just voted to send
stimulus checks to murderers,

00:09:30.302 --> 00:09:31.804
rapists, child molesters,

00:09:31.804 --> 00:09:37.143
Chuckys, Jasons, Xenomorphs,
Freddy Kruegers, and Kuatos."

00:09:37.143 --> 00:09:39.878
Second, I love his sociopathic
little chuckle at the end there.

00:09:39.878 --> 00:09:41.713
Millions out of work,
in poverty,

00:09:41.713 --> 00:09:44.283
facing food insecurity,
and it's all so funny to him --

00:09:44.283 --> 00:09:45.951
or maybe it was just remembering

00:09:45.951 --> 00:09:48.587
when he grabbed the maracas away
from a mariachi

00:09:48.587 --> 00:09:50.389
at the Señor Frogs in Cancun.

00:09:50.389 --> 00:09:53.992
So Democrats stuck together
to fend off GOP stonewalling

00:09:53.992 --> 00:09:55.427
and passed a historic
relief bill

00:09:55.427 --> 00:09:57.262
that could not come
at a more precarious time.

00:09:57.262 --> 00:10:00.799
We're currently in what may well
be a crossroads in the pandemic.

00:10:00.799 --> 00:10:03.302
There's lots of good news,
but also some bad news.

00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:06.538
Vaccinations are accelerating at
a previously unthinkable pace,

00:10:06.538 --> 00:10:09.808
with nearly 3 million doses
administered on Saturday alone.

00:10:09.808 --> 00:10:12.544
Cases have fallen as
dramatically as they ever have

00:10:12.544 --> 00:10:13.945
since the peak in January.

00:10:13.945 --> 00:10:16.816
But cases also now
seem to be plateauing

00:10:16.816 --> 00:10:20.018
at a stubbornly high number
of 60 to 70 thousand per day,

00:10:20.018 --> 00:10:22.254
which leaves more
than enough virus circulating

00:10:22.254 --> 00:10:24.356
for one more deadly
outbreak before summer,

00:10:24.356 --> 00:10:27.426
and yet several states are
racing to prematurely lift

00:10:27.426 --> 00:10:29.528
mask mandates
or open up entirely,

00:10:29.528 --> 00:10:31.964
from Texas to Mississippi,
Alabama, and even Connecticut,

00:10:31.964 --> 00:10:34.033
where the mask mandate
will remain in effect,

00:10:34.033 --> 00:10:36.201
but capacity limits
will be lifted on retail,

00:10:36.201 --> 00:10:37.336
restaurants, and gyms.

00:10:37.336 --> 00:10:39.672
Why would you
lift capacity on gyms?

00:10:39.672 --> 00:10:42.274
The whole business model for
gyms is that people join them

00:10:42.274 --> 00:10:44.477
and then don't go.
It's just a key fob

00:10:44.477 --> 00:10:46.745
that costs $100 a month
to carry around.

00:10:46.745 --> 00:10:48.814
There should be capacity
limits on gyms

00:10:48.814 --> 00:10:50.148
even when there isn't
a pandemic.

00:10:50.148 --> 00:10:52.384
No one wants to change
into running shoes

00:10:52.384 --> 00:10:55.354
right next to one of those
weirdly jacked 80-year-olds

00:10:55.354 --> 00:10:56.789
air-drying his [bleep].

00:10:56.789 --> 00:11:00.926
"Bad things happen
when I put it away wet."

00:11:00.926 --> 00:11:04.897
Stay out of my space, grandpa.

00:11:04.897 --> 00:11:06.865
Now's not the time to take
our foot off the gas --

00:11:06.865 --> 00:11:08.834
if we just hunker down and spend
the next month or two

00:11:08.834 --> 00:11:11.737
crushin' this thing, combined
with the ramped-up vaccinations,

00:11:11.737 --> 00:11:13.071
we can have potentially
a great summer.

00:11:13.071 --> 00:11:15.140
Think about it.
We could have block parties,

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:16.808
neighborhood barbecues,
street fairs.

00:11:16.808 --> 00:11:19.011
Do you remember street fairs
in New York?

00:11:19.011 --> 00:11:21.913
You'd be in a cab in a rush
heading to your apartment

00:11:21.913 --> 00:11:23.549
and all of a sudden
the road would be closed

00:11:23.549 --> 00:11:27.620
and you'd say, "Ah!
[Bleep] street fairs!"

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:30.823
We can have that back soon.

00:11:30.823 --> 00:11:33.559
And yet if you express any
caution or hesitation at all

00:11:33.559 --> 00:11:36.361
about opening up too quickly
in the hopes that we'll be able

00:11:36.361 --> 00:11:38.397
to crush this thing
by summer, Fox News,

00:11:38.397 --> 00:11:40.665
the same people who spread lies
about everything from masks

00:11:40.665 --> 00:11:42.935
to social distancing to
lockdowns

00:11:42.935 --> 00:11:46.338
to the COVID death toll to
vaccines to scam miracle cures,

00:11:46.338 --> 00:11:49.474
had the gall to accuse you
of being pro-pandemic.

00:11:49.474 --> 00:11:53.278
-We might be out of the pandemic
by summer, medically.

00:11:53.278 --> 00:11:54.580
We'll see how long it will
take us to get out

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:56.015
of the pandemic politically.

00:11:56.015 --> 00:11:59.317
Dr. Siegel, thanks so much for
telling us about this new point.

00:11:59.317 --> 00:12:02.088
-Great point, Will.
There's plenty of people

00:12:02.088 --> 00:12:03.622
that want that pandemic
to continue,

00:12:03.622 --> 00:12:05.691
but it is not us.
Thanks for having me.

00:12:05.691 --> 00:12:06.925
-Exactly.

00:12:06.925 --> 00:12:08.394
-Are you out of your [bleep]
mind? Nobody wants

00:12:08.394 --> 00:12:10.529
this godforsaken pandemic
to go on any longer.

00:12:10.529 --> 00:12:12.264
We've all been trapped inside
for a year.

00:12:12.264 --> 00:12:13.765
Forget going to gyms
or movie theaters,

00:12:13.765 --> 00:12:15.934
I'd give anything to be
on a packed "F" train right now

00:12:15.934 --> 00:12:18.304
without air conditioning,
getting crushed on one side

00:12:18.304 --> 00:12:20.505
by a guy with a bike
and the other side by a guy

00:12:20.505 --> 00:12:21.840
with a lizard on his shoulders.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:24.276
This is the central story
of our politics right now.

00:12:24.276 --> 00:12:26.478
One political coalition,
for all its faults,

00:12:26.478 --> 00:12:28.047
is focused on
actually governing,

00:12:28.047 --> 00:12:30.048
and the other has become
unmoored from reality

00:12:30.048 --> 00:12:33.118
and fueled entirely by imagined
cultural grievances over

00:12:33.118 --> 00:12:35.087
everything from children's books
to "The Muppets."

00:12:35.087 --> 00:12:37.489
And with a few exceptions,
Republicans have made

00:12:37.489 --> 00:12:39.658
the conscious decision
to lean into that.

00:12:39.658 --> 00:12:41.660
They've made
the cynical calculation

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:43.928
that sticking with a racist,
authoritarian criminal

00:12:43.928 --> 00:12:45.330
who sowed an insurrection

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:47.799
to overthrow democracy
is the path to power.

00:12:47.799 --> 00:12:49.835
Senator Lindsey Graham
told Axios last night

00:12:49.835 --> 00:12:52.537
he's trying to harness the
energy of the Trump movement.

00:12:52.537 --> 00:12:54.906
-There's something about Trump.

00:12:54.906 --> 00:12:59.044
There's a dark side
and there's some magic there.

00:12:59.044 --> 00:13:02.381
And what I'm trying to do
is just harness the magic.

00:13:02.381 --> 00:13:09.154
To me, Donald Trump is sort of
a cross between Jesse Helms,

00:13:09.154 --> 00:13:11.156
Ronald Reagan, and P.T. Barnum.

00:13:11.156 --> 00:13:13.358
-And that sounds like
a good combination to you?

00:13:13.358 --> 00:13:14.726
Who else were you
going to include?

00:13:14.726 --> 00:13:16.161
John Gotti and
Jabba the Hutt?

00:13:16.161 --> 00:13:18.097
Also, what do you mean,
you want to "harness the magic?"

00:13:18.097 --> 00:13:20.331
You sound like
a regional theater director

00:13:20.331 --> 00:13:22.367
trying to whip your cast
into shape

00:13:22.367 --> 00:13:24.068
for a production of "Our Town."

00:13:24.068 --> 00:13:25.937
[ Southern accent ]
"Come on, people. You were
supposed to practice

00:13:25.937 --> 00:13:27.773
these dance numbers
on your own time.

00:13:27.773 --> 00:13:29.908
You need to stop whining
and harness the magic,

00:13:29.908 --> 00:13:31.910
or else my Mee-maw's
is going to keep telling me

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:33.578
I wasn't cut out for Broadway.

00:13:33.578 --> 00:13:37.849
At least I have dreams,
Mee-maw!"

00:13:37.849 --> 00:13:39.117
The majority of
House Republicans

00:13:39.117 --> 00:13:41.253
voted to overturn
the November election results,

00:13:41.253 --> 00:13:43.789
and not a single one of them
voted to fund vaccinations

00:13:43.789 --> 00:13:46.192
and send urgently-needed relief
to the American people

00:13:46.192 --> 00:13:48.126
amid a pandemic
and economic crash.

00:13:48.126 --> 00:13:50.863
That simple fact should tell
you everything you need to know

00:13:50.863 --> 00:13:52.564
about the state of our politics.

00:13:52.564 --> 00:13:54.466
Whatever their flaws, the
Democrats' message

00:13:54.466 --> 00:13:56.301
to voters is this.
"Do you like checks?

00:13:56.301 --> 00:13:57.670
Do you like
unemployment benefits?

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.804
Do you like money for children,
schools,

00:13:59.804 --> 00:14:01.106
vaccines, and pensioners?"

00:14:01.106 --> 00:14:03.141
And the Republicans' message
to voters is,

00:14:03.141 --> 00:14:05.410
-"Do you like green eggs and
ham?"

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:07.346
-This has been a closer look.

00:14:07.346 --> 00:14:10.782
♪♪

00:14:10.782 --> 00:14:12.217
God's Love We Deliver cooks
and brings

00:14:12.217 --> 00:14:14.286
over two million meals a year to
men, women and children

00:14:14.286 --> 00:14:17.022
living with HIV, AIDS, cancer,
and other serious illnesses,

00:14:17.022 --> 00:14:18.523
and they need your help.

00:14:18.523 --> 00:14:20.225
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the donate button.

00:14:20.225 --> 00:14:23.229
Stay safe, wear a mask,
get vaccinated. We love you.

